window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b195-0dd6881e42bf3806.json"]={sha256:"0dd6881e42bf3806b3a6b978c2e746fd3aac916deb9b07374a631da1799f2968",value:{"id":"b195","title":"隧道耐震接頭設計","titleEn":"Seismic tunnel-joint design","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦以相對位移、接頭剛度與止水餘量理解隧道耐震接頭。十個單元依序辨識作用機制、量化假設、驗證程序與故障徵兆，讓學徒追蹤從原始資料到工程判斷的每一環。每個算例都帶單位與限制，不把局部成功或單一比值當成完整系統合格。交接須保留基準、異常與權責工程師核准的條件。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on understand seismic tunnel joints through relative movement, joint stiffness and sealing reserve. Ten units connect mechanisms, numerical assumptions, verification procedures and failure symptoms so apprentices can trace each inference from evidence to judgment. Every example includes units and limitations; one successful observation or ratio does not establish system acceptance. Handover retains datums, anomalies and conditions approved by the responsible engineer.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-ground","subcategoryTitle":"地盤改良與地下維護","subcategoryTitleEn":"Ground improvement and underground maintenance","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-ground","learningTags":["underground","ug-ground","ground"],"architectureFamily":"ground","architectureNodes":[["波傳軸向應變","Wave induced axial strain"],["接頭剪切剛度","Joint shear stiffness"],["止水壓縮幾何餘量","Seal compression geometry reserve"],["斷層變形帶需求","Fault deformation band demand"],["位移容量與交接","Movement capacity and handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[3,1]],"diagram":{"type":"ground","labels":["波傳軸向應變","接頭剪切剛度","止水壓縮幾何餘量","斷層變形帶需求","位移容量與交接"],"labelsEn":["Wave induced axial strain","Joint shear stiffness","Seal compression geometry reserve","Fault deformation band demand","Movement capacity and handover"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創教學算例，所有輸入均為假設，不是地標實測。教學假設，非現場設定值：假設沿隧道方向的適用平面波粒子速度v=0.50m/s、對應波速c=500m/s，ε=v/c=0.001；不能代入任意方向的總峰值。假設指定方向粒子速度由0.50增加10%至0.55m/s，對應波速固定500m/s，應變由0.001增為0.0011；同一20m分配長度的位移由20增至22mm。此結果須維持波型、方向與分配邊界相同。先列出符號、單位及固定條件，再以獨立計算器核算。敏感度只描述這個模型中的輸入改變；若邊界或物理機制改變，應重建模型而非線性外推。最後把計算值、量測不確定性及需進一步驗證的項目分列，由責任工程師決定能否支持下一階段。","textEn":"The following original example uses assumptions rather than landmark measurements. Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an appropriate plane wave along the tunnel, particle velocity v=0.50m/s and corresponding c=500m/s give ε=0.001. An arbitrary total peak is unsuitable. Increasing assumed directional particle velocity from0.50 to0.55m/s by10% at corresponding speed500m/s changes strain from0.001 to0.0011. Over the same20m allocation length, movement rises from20 to22mm. Wave type, direction and allocation boundaries must remain unchanged. First tabulate symbols, units and fixed conditions, then check the arithmetic independently. Sensitivity describes an input change inside this model only. Changed boundaries or physical mechanisms require a new model rather than linear extrapolation. Finally distinguish the calculated result, measurement uncertainty and evidence still needed; the responsible engineer decides whether the conclusion supports a next stage.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b195-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「波傳軸向應變」與「接頭相對伸長」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wave induced axial strain\" and \"Joint relative extension\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b195-v14-01","title":"波傳軸向應變：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wave induced axial strain: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「波傳軸向應變」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wave induced axial strain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地下結構受地震波強迫變形，和地面建物單看慣性力的模型不同。沿隧道方向的簡化平面波可用粒子速度與對應波速估應變，但必須指定方向及波型。假設沿隧道方向的適用平面波粒子速度v=0.50m/s、對應波速c=500m/s，ε=v/c=0.001；不能代入任意方向的總峰值。若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波傳軸向應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Seismic waves impose ground deformation on tunnels, unlike a model considering only building inertia. A simplified wave along the tunnel relates particle velocity to the corresponding wave speed, requiring an explicit direction and wave type. For an appropriate plane wave along the tunnel, particle velocity v=0.50m/s and corresponding c=500m/s give ε=0.001. An arbitrary total peak is unsuitable. Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain. Stiff-soft transitions can also concentrate displacement, so a mean wave model may miss the joint controlling actual performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave induced axial strain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設沿隧道方向的適用平面波粒子速度v=0.50m/s、對應波速c=500m/s，ε=v/c=0.001；不能代入任意方向的總峰值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an appropriate plane wave along the tunnel, particle velocity v=0.50m/s and corresponding c=500m/s give ε=0.001.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「波傳軸向應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave induced axial strain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-01-k1","title":"波傳軸向應變","titleEn":"Wave induced axial strain","text":"地下結構受地震波強迫變形，和地面建物單看慣性力的模型不同。沿隧道方向的簡化平面波可用粒子速度與對應波速估應變，但必須指定方向及波型。","textEn":"Seismic waves impose ground deformation on tunnels, unlike a model considering only building inertia. A simplified wave along the tunnel relates particle velocity to the corresponding wave speed, requiring an explicit direction and wave type.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「波傳軸向應變」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wave induced axial strain\" is correct?","options":["只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","地下結構受地震波強迫變形，和地面建物單看慣性力的模型不同。","只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Seismic waves impose ground deformation on tunnels, unlike a model considering only building inertia.","A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地下結構受地震波強迫變形，和地面建物單看慣性力的模型不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Seismic waves impose ground deformation on tunnels, unlike a model considering only building inertia. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b195-v14-02","title":"波傳軸向應變：定量估算","titleEn":"Wave induced axial strain: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「波傳軸向應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wave induced axial strain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設沿隧道方向的適用平面波粒子速度v=0.50m/s、對應波速c=500m/s，ε=v/c=0.001；不能代入任意方向的總峰值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an appropriate plane wave along the tunnel, particle velocity v=0.50m/s and corresponding c=500m/s give ε=0.001. An arbitrary total peak is unsuitable. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對地震輸入的方向、波型與波速剖面，將自由場應變和土結互制分析比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check input direction, wave type and velocity profile, comparing free-field strain with interaction analysis.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設沿隧道方向的適用平面波粒子速度v=0.50m/s、對應波速c=500m/s，ε=v/c=0.001；不能代入任意方向的總峰值。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an appropriate plane wave along the tunnel, particle velocity v=0.50m/s and corresponding c=500m/s give ε=0.001. An arbitrary total peak is unsuitable.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「波傳軸向應變」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wave induced axial strain\", which statement holds?","options":["只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","教學假設，非現場設定值：假設沿隧道方向的適用平面波粒子速度v=0.50m/s、對應波速c=500m/s，ε=v/c=0.001；不能代入任意方向的總峰值。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an appropriate plane wave along the tunnel, particle velocity v=0.50m/s and corresponding c=500m/s give ε=0.001."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設沿隧道方向的適用平面波粒子速度v=0.50m/s、對應波速c=500m/s，ε=v/c=0.001；不能代入任意方向的總峰值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an appropriate plane wave along the tunnel, particle velocity v=0.50m/s and corresponding c=500m/s give ε=0.001. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b195-v14-03","title":"波傳軸向應變：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wave induced axial strain: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「波傳軸向應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wave induced axial strain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對地震輸入的方向、波型與波速剖面，將自由場應變和土結互制分析比較。對斜交波及地層變化保留專門分析，不把此式當所有地震情境的包絡值。同時排除以下干擾原因：若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check input direction, wave type and velocity profile, comparing free-field strain with interaction analysis. Oblique waves and stratigraphic transitions require specific treatment; the relation is not a universal seismic envelope. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain. Stiff-soft transitions can also concentrate displacement, so a mean wave model may miss the joint controlling actual performance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接波傳軸向應變時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。核對地震輸入的方向、波型與波速剖面，將自由場應變和土結互制分析比較。對斜交波及地層變化保留專門分析，不把此式當所有地震情境的包絡值。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over wave induced axial strain, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Check input direction, wave type and velocity profile, comparing free-field strain with interaction analysis. Oblique waves and stratigraphic transitions require specific treatment; the relation is not a universal seismic envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對地震輸入的方向、波型與波速剖面，將自由場應變和土結互制分析比較。對斜交波及地層變化保留專門分析，不把此式當所有地震情境的包絡值。同時排除以下干擾原因：若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。","textEn":"Check input direction, wave type and velocity profile, comparing free-field strain with interaction analysis. Oblique waves and stratigraphic transitions require specific treatment; the relation is not a universal seismic envelope. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain. Stiff-soft transitions can also concentrate displacement, so a mean wave model may miss the joint controlling actual performance.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接波傳軸向應變時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。核對地震輸入的方向、波型與波速剖面，將自由場應變和土結互制分析比較。對斜交波及地層變化保留專門分析，不把此式當所有地震情境的包絡值。","textEn":"When handing over wave induced axial strain, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Check input direction, wave type and velocity profile, comparing free-field strain with interaction analysis. Oblique waves and stratigraphic transitions require specific treatment; the relation is not a universal seismic envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「波傳軸向應變」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wave induced axial strain\"?","options":["核對地震輸入的方向、波型與波速剖面，將自由場應變和土結互制分析比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Check input direction, wave type and velocity profile, comparing free-field strain with interaction analysis.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對地震輸入的方向、波型與波速剖面，將自由場應變和土結互制分析比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check input direction, wave type and velocity profile, comparing free-field strain with interaction analysis. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b195-v14-04","title":"波傳軸向應變：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wave induced axial strain: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「波傳軸向應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wave induced axial strain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain. Stiff-soft transitions can also concentrate displacement, so a mean wave model may miss the joint controlling actual performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Stiff-soft transitions can also concentrate displacement, so a mean wave model may miss the joint controlling actual performance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。","textEn":"Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain. Stiff-soft transitions can also concentrate displacement, so a mean wave model may miss the joint controlling actual performance.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「波傳軸向應變」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wave induced axial strain\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。","只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain.","A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若將剪波速度搭配無關方向的粒子速度，應變需求可被誤估；硬軟地層交界又可集中相對位移，平均波傳模型可能漏掉真正控制的接頭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Combining shear-wave speed with unrelated particle motion misestimates strain. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b195-v14-05","title":"接頭相對伸長：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint relative extension: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「接頭相對伸長」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint relative extension” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"軸向地盤應變在一段長度上累積成位移，但並非全部都集中在單一接頭。襯砌軸向剛度、地盤摩擦及接頭分布共同決定分配，簡式只是指定分攤情境。假設ε=0.001均勻作用於L=20m且這段變形分配給所查接頭，Δ=εL=0.020m即20mm；實際分配另算。若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接頭相對伸長」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Axial ground strain accumulates over length but does not necessarily concentrate at one joint. Lining stiffness, ground friction and joint distribution govern sharing; the simple relation represents a specified allocation scenario. If ε=0.001 acts uniformly over L=20m and that segment's deformation is allocated to the checked joint, Δ=0.020m, or20mm; real sharing needs analysis. Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand. Uniform sharing can instead understate opening at an unusually flexible joint and miss loss of water sealing. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint relative extension” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設ε=0.001均勻作用於L=20m且這段變形分配給所查接頭，Δ=εL=0.020m即20mm；實際分配另算。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: If ε=0.001 acts uniformly over L=20m and that segment's deformation is allocated to the checked joint, Δ=0.020m, or20mm; real sharing needs analysis.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接頭相對伸長」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint relative extension”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-05-k1","title":"接頭相對伸長","titleEn":"Joint relative extension","text":"軸向地盤應變在一段長度上累積成位移，但並非全部都集中在單一接頭。襯砌軸向剛度、地盤摩擦及接頭分布共同決定分配，簡式只是指定分攤情境。","textEn":"Axial ground strain accumulates over length but does not necessarily concentrate at one joint. Lining stiffness, ground friction and joint distribution govern sharing; the simple relation represents a specified allocation scenario.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭相對伸長」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint relative extension\" is correct?","options":["只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","軸向地盤應變在一段長度上累積成位移，但並非全部都集中在單一接頭。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Axial ground strain accumulates over length but does not necessarily concentrate at one joint."],"answer":2,"explanation":"軸向地盤應變在一段長度上累積成位移，但並非全部都集中在單一接頭。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Axial ground strain accumulates over length but does not necessarily concentrate at one joint. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b195-v14-06","title":"接頭相對伸長：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint relative extension: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接頭相對伸長」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint relative extension” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設ε=0.001均勻作用於L=20m且這段變形分配給所查接頭，Δ=εL=0.020m即20mm；實際分配另算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: If ε=0.001 acts uniformly over L=20m and that segment's deformation is allocated to the checked joint, Δ=0.020m, or20mm; real sharing needs analysis. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將環縫與縱向接頭位置畫成變形相容圖，檢查位移和襯砌伸長的總和。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map circumferential and longitudinal joints in a compatibility diagram, checking the sum of joint movement and lining extension.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設ε=0.001均勻作用於L=20m且這段變形分配給所查接頭，Δ=εL=0.020m即20mm；實際分配另算。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: If ε=0.001 acts uniformly over L=20m and that segment's deformation is allocated to the checked joint, Δ=0.020m, or20mm; real sharing needs analysis.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭相對伸長」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint relative extension\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非現場設定值：假設ε=0.001均勻作用於L=20m且這段變形分配給所查接頭，Δ=εL=0.020m即20mm；實際分配另算。","只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not field settings: If ε=0.001 acts uniformly over L=20m and that segment's deformation is allocated to the checked joint, Δ=0.020m, or20mm.","A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設ε=0.001均勻作用於L=20m且這段變形分配給所查接頭，Δ=εL=0.020m即20mm；實際分配另算。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: If ε=0.001 acts uniformly over L=20m and that segment's deformation is allocated to the checked joint, Δ=0.020m, or20mm; real sharing needs analysis. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b195-v14-07","title":"接頭相對伸長：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint relative extension: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接頭相對伸長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint relative extension” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將環縫與縱向接頭位置畫成變形相容圖，檢查位移和襯砌伸長的總和。比較接頭量測及模型結果，對端部、剛度變化與特殊構造另設控制點。同時排除以下干擾原因：若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map circumferential and longitudinal joints in a compatibility diagram, checking the sum of joint movement and lining extension. Compare measured and modelled response at ends, stiffness changes and special structures. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand. Uniform sharing can instead understate opening at an unusually flexible joint and miss loss of water sealing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接接頭相對伸長時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。將環縫與縱向接頭位置畫成變形相容圖，檢查位移和襯砌伸長的總和。比較接頭量測及模型結果，對端部、剛度變化與特殊構造另設控制點。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over joint relative extension, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Map circumferential and longitudinal joints in a compatibility diagram, checking the sum of joint movement and lining extension. Compare measured and modelled response at ends, stiffness changes and special structures.","failure":"注意干擾：若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將環縫與縱向接頭位置畫成變形相容圖，檢查位移和襯砌伸長的總和。比較接頭量測及模型結果，對端部、剛度變化與特殊構造另設控制點。同時排除以下干擾原因：若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。","textEn":"Map circumferential and longitudinal joints in a compatibility diagram, checking the sum of joint movement and lining extension. Compare measured and modelled response at ends, stiffness changes and special structures. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand. Uniform sharing can instead understate opening at an unusually flexible joint and miss loss of water sealing.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接接頭相對伸長時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。將環縫與縱向接頭位置畫成變形相容圖，檢查位移和襯砌伸長的總和。比較接頭量測及模型結果，對端部、剛度變化與特殊構造另設控制點。","textEn":"When handing over joint relative extension, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Map circumferential and longitudinal joints in a compatibility diagram, checking the sum of joint movement and lining extension. Compare measured and modelled response at ends, stiffness changes and special structures.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭相對伸長」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint relative extension\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將環縫與縱向接頭位置畫成變形相容圖，檢查位移和襯砌伸長的總和。","只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Map circumferential and longitudinal joints in a compatibility diagram, checking the sum of joint movement and lining extension.","A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將環縫與縱向接頭位置畫成變形相容圖，檢查位移和襯砌伸長的總和。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map circumferential and longitudinal joints in a compatibility diagram, checking the sum of joint movement and lining extension. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b195-v14-08","title":"接頭相對伸長：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint relative extension: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接頭相對伸長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint relative extension” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand. Uniform sharing can instead understate opening at an unusually flexible joint and miss loss of water sealing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uniform sharing can instead understate opening at an unusually flexible joint and miss loss of water sealing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。","textEn":"Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand. Uniform sharing can instead understate opening at an unusually flexible joint and miss loss of water sealing.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭相對伸長」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint relative extension\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若把全長地盤位移同時分配到每一接頭，會重複計算需求；若反過來平均分攤而忽略一處特別柔軟，則可能低估該處張開與止水破壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Allocating total tunnel displacement to every joint double counts demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b195-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「接頭剪切剛度」與「轉角邊緣張開」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint shear stiffness\" and \"Rotation induced edge opening\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b195-v14-09","title":"接頭剪切剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint shear stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「接頭剪切剛度」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint shear stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"接頭剪切剛度決定位移引起的力，柔性接頭能減少某些力卻可能增加位移與密封需求。線性彈簧只代表特定範圍，間隙、摩擦滑移及損傷會改變關係。假設剪切剛度k=50MN/m、相對位移Δ=0.010m，V=kΔ=0.50MN；此為線性範圍的力，不是接頭剪力容量。若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接頭剪切剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joint shear stiffness converts movement to force. Flexibility may reduce force while increasing displacement and sealing demand; a linear spring applies only within a range, before gaps, frictional slip or damage change behaviour. For shear stiffness k=50MN/m and Δ=0.010m, V=kΔ=0.50MN. This is linear-range demand, not joint shear capacity. Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force. Conversely, residual slip may exceed sealing capacity even when the calculated force falls, so one favourable response measure is insufficient. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint shear stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設剪切剛度k=50MN/m、相對位移Δ=0.010m，V=kΔ=0.50MN；此為線性範圍的力，不是接頭剪力容量。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For shear stiffness k=50MN/m and Δ=0.010m, V=kΔ=0.50MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接頭剪切剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint shear stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-09-k1","title":"接頭剪切剛度","titleEn":"Joint shear stiffness","text":"接頭剪切剛度決定位移引起的力，柔性接頭能減少某些力卻可能增加位移與密封需求。線性彈簧只代表特定範圍，間隙、摩擦滑移及損傷會改變關係。","textEn":"Joint shear stiffness converts movement to force. Flexibility may reduce force while increasing displacement and sealing demand; a linear spring applies only within a range, before gaps, frictional slip or damage change behaviour.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭剪切剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint shear stiffness\" is correct?","options":["接頭剪切剛度決定位移引起的力，柔性接頭能減少某些力卻可能增加位移與密封需求。","只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Joint shear stiffness converts movement to force.","A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭剪切剛度決定位移引起的力，柔性接頭能減少某些力卻可能增加位移與密封需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joint shear stiffness converts movement to force. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b195-v14-10","title":"接頭剪切剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint shear stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接頭剪切剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint shear stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設剪切剛度k=50MN/m、相對位移Δ=0.010m，V=kΔ=0.50MN；此為線性範圍的力，不是接頭剪力容量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For shear stiffness k=50MN/m and Δ=0.010m, V=kΔ=0.50MN. This is linear-range demand, not joint shear capacity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用代表性接頭試驗確認力位移曲線、循環退化與溫度條件，將軸向壓力也列入比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test representative force-displacement response, cyclic degradation and temperature, including axial loading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設剪切剛度k=50MN/m、相對位移Δ=0.010m，V=kΔ=0.50MN；此為線性範圍的力，不是接頭剪力容量。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For shear stiffness k=50MN/m and Δ=0.010m, V=kΔ=0.50MN. This is linear-range demand, not joint shear capacity.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭剪切剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint shear stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","教學假設，非現場設定值：假設剪切剛度k=50MN/m、相對位移Δ=0.010m，V=kΔ=0.50MN；此為線性範圍的力，不是接頭剪力容量。","只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For shear stiffness k=50MN/m and Δ=0.010m, V=kΔ=0.50MN.","A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設剪切剛度k=50MN/m、相對位移Δ=0.010m，V=kΔ=0.50MN；此為線性範圍的力，不是接頭剪力容量。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For shear stiffness k=50MN/m and Δ=0.010m, V=kΔ=0.50MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b195-v14-11","title":"接頭剪切剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint shear stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接頭剪切剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint shear stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用代表性接頭試驗確認力位移曲線、循環退化與溫度條件，將軸向壓力也列入比較。設計須同時檢查力、位移及密封，不能只降低剛度求較小內力。同時排除以下干擾原因：若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test representative force-displacement response, cyclic degradation and temperature, including axial loading. Check force, movement and sealing together rather than selecting low stiffness solely to reduce calculated force. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force. Conversely, residual slip may exceed sealing capacity even when the calculated force falls, so one favourable response measure is insufficient. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接接頭剪切剛度時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。用代表性接頭試驗確認力位移曲線、循環退化與溫度條件，將軸向壓力也列入比較。設計須同時檢查力、位移及密封，不能只降低剛度求較小內力。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over joint shear stiffness, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Test representative force-displacement response, cyclic degradation and temperature, including axial loading. Check force, movement and sealing together rather than selecting low stiffness solely to reduce calculated force.","failure":"注意干擾：若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用代表性接頭試驗確認力位移曲線、循環退化與溫度條件，將軸向壓力也列入比較。設計須同時檢查力、位移及密封，不能只降低剛度求較小內力。同時排除以下干擾原因：若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。","textEn":"Test representative force-displacement response, cyclic degradation and temperature, including axial loading. Check force, movement and sealing together rather than selecting low stiffness solely to reduce calculated force. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force. Conversely, residual slip may exceed sealing capacity even when the calculated force falls, so one favourable response measure is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接接頭剪切剛度時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。用代表性接頭試驗確認力位移曲線、循環退化與溫度條件，將軸向壓力也列入比較。設計須同時檢查力、位移及密封，不能只降低剛度求較小內力。","textEn":"When handing over joint shear stiffness, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Test representative force-displacement response, cyclic degradation and temperature, including axial loading. Check force, movement and sealing together rather than selecting low stiffness solely to reduce calculated force.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭剪切剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint shear stiffness\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","用代表性接頭試驗確認力位移曲線、循環退化與溫度條件，將軸向壓力也列入比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Test representative force-displacement response, cyclic degradation and temperature, including axial loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用代表性接頭試驗確認力位移曲線、循環退化與溫度條件，將軸向壓力也列入比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test representative force-displacement response, cyclic degradation and temperature, including axial loading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b195-v14-12","title":"接頭剪切剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint shear stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接頭剪切剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint shear stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force. Conversely, residual slip may exceed sealing capacity even when the calculated force falls, so one favourable response measure is insufficient. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Conversely, residual slip may exceed sealing capacity even when the calculated force falls, so one favourable response measure is insufficient.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。","textEn":"Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force. Conversely, residual slip may exceed sealing capacity even when the calculated force falls, so one favourable response measure is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭剪切剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint shear stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若模型忽略接觸閉合後剛度突然升高，峰值力可能被低估；相反，滑移後殘餘變形也可能超出止水能力，即使計算內力看似下降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring sudden stiffness increase after contact can understate peak force. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b195-v14-13","title":"轉角邊緣張開：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rotation induced edge opening: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「轉角邊緣張開」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rotation induced edge opening” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"接頭轉角會使截面邊緣相對張開，中心位移很小也可能在外緣造成止水需求。小角近似適用於指定旋轉軸，實際多軸運動需組合而不能只採單一截面。假設轉角θ=0.002rad、距旋轉軸R=4m，邊緣位移Δedge≈θR=0.008m即8mm；正負端方向相反。單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉角邊緣張開」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joint rotation opens edges even when centre movement is small. A small-angle approximation needs a defined axis; multi-axis motion requires combination rather than one section's result. For θ=0.002rad and distance R=4m from the rotation axis, Δedge≈θR=0.008m, or8mm, with opposite signs on opposite edges. A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening. Uniform seal compression assumptions conceal simultaneous contact loss on one side and excessive compression on the other. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rotation induced edge opening” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設轉角θ=0.002rad、距旋轉軸R=4m，邊緣位移Δedge≈θR=0.008m即8mm；正負端方向相反。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For θ=0.002rad and distance R=4m from the rotation axis, Δedge≈θR=0.008m, or8mm, with opposite signs on opposite edges.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「轉角邊緣張開」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rotation induced edge opening”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-13-k1","title":"轉角邊緣張開","titleEn":"Rotation induced edge opening","text":"接頭轉角會使截面邊緣相對張開，中心位移很小也可能在外緣造成止水需求。小角近似適用於指定旋轉軸，實際多軸運動需組合而不能只採單一截面。","textEn":"Joint rotation opens edges even when centre movement is small. A small-angle approximation needs a defined axis; multi-axis motion requires combination rather than one section's result.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「轉角邊緣張開」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rotation induced edge opening\" is correct?","options":["只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","接頭轉角會使截面邊緣相對張開，中心位移很小也可能在外緣造成止水需求。","只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Joint rotation opens edges even when centre movement is small.","A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接頭轉角會使截面邊緣相對張開，中心位移很小也可能在外緣造成止水需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joint rotation opens edges even when centre movement is small. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b195-v14-14","title":"轉角邊緣張開：定量估算","titleEn":"Rotation induced edge opening: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「轉角邊緣張開」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rotation induced edge opening” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設轉角θ=0.002rad、距旋轉軸R=4m，邊緣位移Δedge≈θR=0.008m即8mm；正負端方向相反。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For θ=0.002rad and distance R=4m from the rotation axis, Δedge≈θR=0.008m, or8mm, with opposite signs on opposite edges. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用至少可辨識轉動的多點位移配置，將剛體平移與旋轉分開擬合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use multiple displacement points to distinguish rigid translation and rotation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設轉角θ=0.002rad、距旋轉軸R=4m，邊緣位移Δedge≈θR=0.008m即8mm；正負端方向相反。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For θ=0.002rad and distance R=4m from the rotation axis, Δedge≈θR=0.008m, or8mm, with opposite signs on opposite edges.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「轉角邊緣張開」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rotation induced edge opening\", which statement holds?","options":["只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","教學假設，非現場設定值：假設轉角θ=0.002rad、距旋轉軸R=4m，邊緣位移Δedge≈θR=0.008m即8mm；正負端方向相反。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For θ=0.002rad and distance R=4m from the rotation axis, Δedge≈θR=0.008m, or8mm, with opposite signs on opposite edges."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設轉角θ=0.002rad、距旋轉軸R=4m，邊緣位移Δedge≈θR=0.008m即8mm；正負端方向相反。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For θ=0.002rad and distance R=4m from the rotation axis, Δedge≈θR=0.008m, or8mm, with opposite signs on opposite edges. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b195-v14-15","title":"轉角邊緣張開：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rotation induced edge opening: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「轉角邊緣張開」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rotation induced edge opening” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用至少可辨識轉動的多點位移配置，將剛體平移與旋轉分開擬合。核對止水所在實際半徑及安裝偏差，再以經核准的多軸試驗包絡確認需求。同時排除以下干擾原因：單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use multiple displacement points to distinguish rigid translation and rotation. Check the actual seal radius and installation tolerance, then compare demand with an approved multiaxis test envelope. Also rule out the following competing explanation: A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening. Uniform seal compression assumptions conceal simultaneous contact loss on one side and excessive compression on the other. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接轉角邊緣張開時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。使用至少可辨識轉動的多點位移配置，將剛體平移與旋轉分開擬合。核對止水所在實際半徑及安裝偏差，再以經核准的多軸試驗包絡確認需求。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over rotation induced edge opening, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Use multiple displacement points to distinguish rigid translation and rotation. Check the actual seal radius and installation tolerance, then compare demand with an approved multiaxis test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用至少可辨識轉動的多點位移配置，將剛體平移與旋轉分開擬合。核對止水所在實際半徑及安裝偏差，再以經核准的多軸試驗包絡確認需求。同時排除以下干擾原因：單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。","textEn":"Use multiple displacement points to distinguish rigid translation and rotation. Check the actual seal radius and installation tolerance, then compare demand with an approved multiaxis test envelope. Also rule out the following competing explanation: A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening. Uniform seal compression assumptions conceal simultaneous contact loss on one side and excessive compression on the other.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接轉角邊緣張開時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。使用至少可辨識轉動的多點位移配置，將剛體平移與旋轉分開擬合。核對止水所在實際半徑及安裝偏差，再以經核准的多軸試驗包絡確認需求。","textEn":"When handing over rotation induced edge opening, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Use multiple displacement points to distinguish rigid translation and rotation. Check the actual seal radius and installation tolerance, then compare demand with an approved multiaxis test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「轉角邊緣張開」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rotation induced edge opening\"?","options":["使用至少可辨識轉動的多點位移配置，將剛體平移與旋轉分開擬合。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Use multiple displacement points to distinguish rigid translation and rotation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用至少可辨識轉動的多點位移配置，將剛體平移與旋轉分開擬合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use multiple displacement points to distinguish rigid translation and rotation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b195-v14-16","title":"轉角邊緣張開：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rotation induced edge opening: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「轉角邊緣張開」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rotation induced edge opening” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening. Uniform seal compression assumptions conceal simultaneous contact loss on one side and excessive compression on the other. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uniform seal compression assumptions conceal simultaneous contact loss on one side and excessive compression on the other.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。","textEn":"A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening. Uniform seal compression assumptions conceal simultaneous contact loss on one side and excessive compression on the other.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「轉角邊緣張開」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rotation induced edge opening\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。","只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening.","A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單點量測若靠近旋轉中心，會低估邊緣開口；假設整條止水帶承受相同壓縮會漏掉一側失去接觸、另一側過度壓縮的同時發生。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A sensor near the rotation centre can miss edge opening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b195-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「止水壓縮幾何餘量」與「連接件局部應變」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Seal compression geometry reserve\" and \"Local connector strain\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b195-v14-17","title":"止水壓縮幾何餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seal compression geometry reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮幾何餘量」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seal compression geometry reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"止水剩餘壓縮量是幾何量，水密性還取決於材料曲線、老化、表面及水壓。幾何仍有接觸不等於接觸壓力足夠，必須用試驗建立容許的運動範圍。假設初始壓縮c0=30mm、接頭張開Δ=12mm，cres=c0−Δ=18mm；沒有材料曲線不能算接觸壓或保證不漏水。止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮幾何餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Remaining seal compression is geometric. Watertightness also depends on material response, ageing, contact surfaces and water pressure. Continued geometric contact does not establish enough contact pressure; testing defines the admissible motion range. For initial compression c0=30mm and opening Δ=12mm, cres=18mm. Without a material curve this cannot determine contact pressure or guarantee watertightness. Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression. A geometric reserve alone misses small flow paths that can develop into leakage under sustained external pressure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seal compression geometry reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設初始壓縮c0=30mm、接頭張開Δ=12mm，cres=c0−Δ=18mm；沒有材料曲線不能算接觸壓或保證不漏水。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For initial compression c0=30mm and opening Δ=12mm, cres=18mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮幾何餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seal compression geometry reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-17-k1","title":"止水壓縮幾何餘量","titleEn":"Seal compression geometry reserve","text":"止水剩餘壓縮量是幾何量，水密性還取決於材料曲線、老化、表面及水壓。幾何仍有接觸不等於接觸壓力足夠，必須用試驗建立容許的運動範圍。","textEn":"Remaining seal compression is geometric. Watertightness also depends on material response, ageing, contact surfaces and water pressure.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「止水壓縮幾何餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seal compression geometry reserve\" is correct?","options":["只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","止水剩餘壓縮量是幾何量，水密性還取決於材料曲線、老化、表面及水壓。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Remaining seal compression is geometric."],"answer":2,"explanation":"止水剩餘壓縮量是幾何量，水密性還取決於材料曲線、老化、表面及水壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Remaining seal compression is geometric. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b195-v14-18","title":"止水壓縮幾何餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Seal compression geometry reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮幾何餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seal compression geometry reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設初始壓縮c0=30mm、接頭張開Δ=12mm，cres=c0−Δ=18mm；沒有材料曲線不能算接觸壓或保證不漏水。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For initial compression c0=30mm and opening Δ=12mm, cres=18mm. Without a material curve this cannot determine contact pressure or guarantee watertightness. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對密封材料批次、初始壓縮與接觸面公差，採具代表水壓和多軸位移的試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify seal batch, initial compression and contact tolerances using representative pressure and multiaxis tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設初始壓縮c0=30mm、接頭張開Δ=12mm，cres=c0−Δ=18mm；沒有材料曲線不能算接觸壓或保證不漏水。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For initial compression c0=30mm and opening Δ=12mm, cres=18mm. Without a material curve this cannot determine contact pressure or guarantee watertightness.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「止水壓縮幾何餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seal compression geometry reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非現場設定值：假設初始壓縮c0=30mm、接頭張開Δ=12mm，cres=c0−Δ=18mm；沒有材料曲線不能算接觸壓或保證不漏水。","只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For initial compression c0=30mm and opening Δ=12mm, cres=18mm.","A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設初始壓縮c0=30mm、接頭張開Δ=12mm，cres=c0−Δ=18mm；沒有材料曲線不能算接觸壓或保證不漏水。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For initial compression c0=30mm and opening Δ=12mm, cres=18mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b195-v14-19","title":"止水壓縮幾何餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seal compression geometry reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮幾何餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seal compression geometry reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對密封材料批次、初始壓縮與接觸面公差，採具代表水壓和多軸位移的試驗。把老化後性能與施工偏差納入包絡，驗收由設計與品質責任人共同簽認。同時排除以下干擾原因：止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify seal batch, initial compression and contact tolerances using representative pressure and multiaxis tests. Include aged performance and installation deviation in the envelope, with design and quality leads jointly accepting evidence. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression. A geometric reserve alone misses small flow paths that can develop into leakage under sustained external pressure. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接止水壓縮幾何餘量時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。核對密封材料批次、初始壓縮與接觸面公差，採具代表水壓和多軸位移的試驗。把老化後性能與施工偏差納入包絡，驗收由設計與品質責任人共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over seal compression geometry reserve, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Verify seal batch, initial compression and contact tolerances using representative pressure and multiaxis tests. Include aged performance and installation deviation in the envelope, with design and quality leads jointly accepting evidence.","failure":"注意干擾：止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對密封材料批次、初始壓縮與接觸面公差，採具代表水壓和多軸位移的試驗。把老化後性能與施工偏差納入包絡，驗收由設計與品質責任人共同簽認。同時排除以下干擾原因：止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。","textEn":"Verify seal batch, initial compression and contact tolerances using representative pressure and multiaxis tests. Include aged performance and installation deviation in the envelope, with design and quality leads jointly accepting evidence. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression. A geometric reserve alone misses small flow paths that can develop into leakage under sustained external pressure.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接止水壓縮幾何餘量時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。核對密封材料批次、初始壓縮與接觸面公差，採具代表水壓和多軸位移的試驗。把老化後性能與施工偏差納入包絡，驗收由設計與品質責任人共同簽認。","textEn":"When handing over seal compression geometry reserve, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Verify seal batch, initial compression and contact tolerances using representative pressure and multiaxis tests. Include aged performance and installation deviation in the envelope, with design and quality leads jointly accepting evidence.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「止水壓縮幾何餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seal compression geometry reserve\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對密封材料批次、初始壓縮與接觸面公差，採具代表水壓和多軸位移的試驗。","只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Verify seal batch, initial compression and contact tolerances using representative pressure and multiaxis tests.","A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對密封材料批次、初始壓縮與接觸面公差，採具代表水壓和多軸位移的試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify seal batch, initial compression and contact tolerances using representative pressure and multiaxis tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b195-v14-20","title":"止水壓縮幾何餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seal compression geometry reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮幾何餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seal compression geometry reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression. A geometric reserve alone misses small flow paths that can develop into leakage under sustained external pressure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A geometric reserve alone misses small flow paths that can develop into leakage under sustained external pressure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。","textEn":"Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression. A geometric reserve alone misses small flow paths that can develop into leakage under sustained external pressure.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「止水壓縮幾何餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seal compression geometry reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression."],"answer":2,"explanation":"止水老化硬化或局部折皺會讓相同壓縮量產生不同接觸狀態；只保留名義幾何餘量可能忽略細小通道，在持續外水壓下逐步發展滲漏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ageing or wrinkles can change contact at the same nominal compression. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b195-v14-21","title":"連接件局部應變：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Local connector strain: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「連接件局部應變」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Local connector strain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"接頭連接件的變形集中於有效自由長度，不能把位移除以整支外觀長度稀釋應變。局部塑性、螺紋及錨定區可能先控制，線性應變估算不能直接當疲勞壽命。假設連接件有效長L=200mm、伸長Δ=2mm，ε=Δ/L=0.010即1%；是否彈性須另看材料與接頭構造。把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「連接件局部應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Connector extension concentrates over the effective free length, not necessarily its full visible length. Plasticity, threads and anchorage may govern; a simple strain estimate is not a fatigue-life calculation. For effective length L=200mm and extension Δ=2mm, ε=0.010, or1%. Elasticity depends separately on material and connection details. Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain. Repeated movement can damage thread roots or connections while overall displacement remains within the nominal stroke. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Local connector strain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設連接件有效長L=200mm、伸長Δ=2mm，ε=Δ/L=0.010即1%；是否彈性須另看材料與接頭構造。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For effective length L=200mm and extension Δ=2mm, ε=0.010, or1%.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「連接件局部應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Local connector strain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-21-k1","title":"連接件局部應變","titleEn":"Local connector strain","text":"接頭連接件的變形集中於有效自由長度，不能把位移除以整支外觀長度稀釋應變。局部塑性、螺紋及錨定區可能先控制，線性應變估算不能直接當疲勞壽命。","textEn":"Connector extension concentrates over the effective free length, not necessarily its full visible length. Plasticity, threads and anchorage may govern; a simple strain estimate is not a fatigue-life calculation.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「連接件局部應變」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Local connector strain\" is correct?","options":["接頭連接件的變形集中於有效自由長度，不能把位移除以整支外觀長度稀釋應變。","只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Connector extension concentrates over the effective free length, not necessarily its full visible length.","A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭連接件的變形集中於有效自由長度，不能把位移除以整支外觀長度稀釋應變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Connector extension concentrates over the effective free length, not necessarily its full visible length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b195-v14-22","title":"連接件局部應變：定量估算","titleEn":"Local connector strain: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「連接件局部應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Local connector strain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設連接件有效長L=200mm、伸長Δ=2mm，ε=Δ/L=0.010即1%；是否彈性須另看材料與接頭構造。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For effective length L=200mm and extension Δ=2mm, ε=0.010, or1%. Elasticity depends separately on material and connection details. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對自由長度、螺紋及錨定段，將應變量測位置與有限元素或接頭試驗比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Review free length, threads and anchorage, comparing strain locations with analysis or joint testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設連接件有效長L=200mm、伸長Δ=2mm，ε=Δ/L=0.010即1%；是否彈性須另看材料與接頭構造。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For effective length L=200mm and extension Δ=2mm, ε=0.010, or1%. Elasticity depends separately on material and connection details.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「連接件局部應變」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Local connector strain\", which statement holds?","options":["只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","教學假設，非現場設定值：假設連接件有效長L=200mm、伸長Δ=2mm，ε=Δ/L=0.010即1%；是否彈性須另看材料與接頭構造。","只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For effective length L=200mm and extension Δ=2mm, ε=0.010, or1%.","A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設連接件有效長L=200mm、伸長Δ=2mm，ε=Δ/L=0.010即1%；是否彈性須另看材料與接頭構造。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For effective length L=200mm and extension Δ=2mm, ε=0.010, or1%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b195-v14-23","title":"連接件局部應變：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Local connector strain: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「連接件局部應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Local connector strain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對自由長度、螺紋及錨定段，將應變量測位置與有限元素或接頭試驗比較。對循環載重記錄殘餘變形與裂縫，不能只看最後一圈的最大力。同時排除以下干擾原因：把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Review free length, threads and anchorage, comparing strain locations with analysis or joint testing. Under cycling, record residual extension and cracking rather than only the maximum force in the final cycle. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain. Repeated movement can damage thread roots or connections while overall displacement remains within the nominal stroke. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接連接件局部應變時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。核對自由長度、螺紋及錨定段，將應變量測位置與有限元素或接頭試驗比較。對循環載重記錄殘餘變形與裂縫，不能只看最後一圈的最大力。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over local connector strain, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Review free length, threads and anchorage, comparing strain locations with analysis or joint testing. Under cycling, record residual extension and cracking rather than only the maximum force in the final cycle.","failure":"注意干擾：把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對自由長度、螺紋及錨定段，將應變量測位置與有限元素或接頭試驗比較。對循環載重記錄殘餘變形與裂縫，不能只看最後一圈的最大力。同時排除以下干擾原因：把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。","textEn":"Review free length, threads and anchorage, comparing strain locations with analysis or joint testing. Under cycling, record residual extension and cracking rather than only the maximum force in the final cycle. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain. Repeated movement can damage thread roots or connections while overall displacement remains within the nominal stroke.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接連接件局部應變時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。核對自由長度、螺紋及錨定段，將應變量測位置與有限元素或接頭試驗比較。對循環載重記錄殘餘變形與裂縫，不能只看最後一圈的最大力。","textEn":"When handing over local connector strain, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Review free length, threads and anchorage, comparing strain locations with analysis or joint testing. Under cycling, record residual extension and cracking rather than only the maximum force in the final cycle.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「連接件局部應變」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Local connector strain\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","核對自由長度、螺紋及錨定段，將應變量測位置與有限元素或接頭試驗比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Review free length, threads and anchorage, comparing strain locations with analysis or joint testing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對自由長度、螺紋及錨定段，將應變量測位置與有限元素或接頭試驗比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Review free length, threads and anchorage, comparing strain locations with analysis or joint testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b195-v14-24","title":"連接件局部應變：失效診斷","titleEn":"Local connector strain: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「連接件局部應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Local connector strain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain. Repeated movement can damage thread roots or connections while overall displacement remains within the nominal stroke. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Repeated movement can damage thread roots or connections while overall displacement remains within the nominal stroke.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。","textEn":"Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain. Repeated movement can damage thread roots or connections while overall displacement remains within the nominal stroke.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「連接件局部應變」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Local connector strain\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把錨固在混凝土中的長度也當可均勻伸長，會低估局部應變；反覆運動可在螺紋根部或接合處累積損傷，即使整體位移仍在名義行程內。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting embedded length as uniformly extensible understates local strain. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b195-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「斷層變形帶需求」與「串聯柔度分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fault deformation band demand\" and \"Series compliance sharing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b195-v14-25","title":"斷層變形帶需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault deformation band demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「斷層變形帶需求」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault deformation band demand” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"永久斷層錯動和振動造成的往復變形不是同一荷載情境，需分別評估。將錯距分攤到變形帶只能提供平均幾何需求，實際局部剪切可能更集中。假設相對錯距Δ=0.50m、分布寬L=20m，平均γ=Δ/L=0.025即2.5%；並非斷層位移的預測公式。若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「斷層變形帶需求」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Permanent fault offset differs from oscillatory shaking and requires a separate scenario. Spreading offset over a deformation band provides only average geometric demand; localized shear may be more concentrated. For assumed offset Δ=0.50m distributed across L=20m, mean γ=0.025, or2.5%. This is not a formula predicting fault displacement. Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance. Even a large single-joint capacity may not accommodate combined shear and rotation before adjacent lining is damaged. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault deformation band demand” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設相對錯距Δ=0.50m、分布寬L=20m，平均γ=Δ/L=0.025即2.5%；並非斷層位移的預測公式。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For assumed offset Δ=0.50m distributed across L=20m, mean γ=0.025, or2.5%.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「斷層變形帶需求」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault deformation band demand”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-25-k1","title":"斷層變形帶需求","titleEn":"Fault deformation band demand","text":"永久斷層錯動和振動造成的往復變形不是同一荷載情境，需分別評估。將錯距分攤到變形帶只能提供平均幾何需求，實際局部剪切可能更集中。","textEn":"Permanent fault offset differs from oscillatory shaking and requires a separate scenario. Spreading offset over a deformation band provides only average geometric demand; localized shear may be more concentrated.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「斷層變形帶需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault deformation band demand\" is correct?","options":["只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","永久斷層錯動和振動造成的往復變形不是同一荷載情境，需分別評估。","只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Permanent fault offset differs from oscillatory shaking and requires a separate scenario.","A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"永久斷層錯動和振動造成的往復變形不是同一荷載情境，需分別評估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Permanent fault offset differs from oscillatory shaking and requires a separate scenario. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b195-v14-26","title":"斷層變形帶需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault deformation band demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷層變形帶需求」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault deformation band demand” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設相對錯距Δ=0.50m、分布寬L=20m，平均γ=Δ/L=0.025即2.5%；並非斷層位移的預測公式。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For assumed offset Δ=0.50m distributed across L=20m, mean γ=0.025, or2.5%. This is not a formula predicting fault displacement. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以地質證據建立可能位置及帶寬情境，將永久位移與動態需求交由結構模型分別處理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define fault location and width scenarios from geological evidence, analysing permanent and dynamic demands separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設相對錯距Δ=0.50m、分布寬L=20m，平均γ=Δ/L=0.025即2.5%；並非斷層位移的預測公式。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For assumed offset Δ=0.50m distributed across L=20m, mean γ=0.025, or2.5%. This is not a formula predicting fault displacement.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「斷層變形帶需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault deformation band demand\", which statement holds?","options":["只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","教學假設，非現場設定值：假設相對錯距Δ=0.50m、分布寬L=20m，平均γ=Δ/L=0.025即2.5%；並非斷層位移的預測公式。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For assumed offset Δ=0.50m distributed across L=20m, mean γ=0.025, or2.5%."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設相對錯距Δ=0.50m、分布寬L=20m，平均γ=Δ/L=0.025即2.5%；並非斷層位移的預測公式。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For assumed offset Δ=0.50m distributed across L=20m, mean γ=0.025, or2.5%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b195-v14-27","title":"斷層變形帶需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault deformation band demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷層變形帶需求」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault deformation band demand” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以地質證據建立可能位置及帶寬情境，將永久位移與動態需求交由結構模型分別處理。特殊接頭或擴挖方案須有專案審查，不能用平均應變替代斷層評估。同時排除以下干擾原因：若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define fault location and width scenarios from geological evidence, analysing permanent and dynamic demands separately. Special joints or enlarged sections need project review rather than an average-strain substitute for fault assessment. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance. Even a large single-joint capacity may not accommodate combined shear and rotation before adjacent lining is damaged. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接斷層變形帶需求時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。以地質證據建立可能位置及帶寬情境，將永久位移與動態需求交由結構模型分別處理。特殊接頭或擴挖方案須有專案審查，不能用平均應變替代斷層評估。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over fault deformation band demand, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Define fault location and width scenarios from geological evidence, analysing permanent and dynamic demands separately. Special joints or enlarged sections need project review rather than an average-strain substitute for fault assessment.","failure":"注意干擾：若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以地質證據建立可能位置及帶寬情境，將永久位移與動態需求交由結構模型分別處理。特殊接頭或擴挖方案須有專案審查，不能用平均應變替代斷層評估。同時排除以下干擾原因：若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。","textEn":"Define fault location and width scenarios from geological evidence, analysing permanent and dynamic demands separately. Special joints or enlarged sections need project review rather than an average-strain substitute for fault assessment. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance. Even a large single-joint capacity may not accommodate combined shear and rotation before adjacent lining is damaged.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接斷層變形帶需求時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。以地質證據建立可能位置及帶寬情境，將永久位移與動態需求交由結構模型分別處理。特殊接頭或擴挖方案須有專案審查，不能用平均應變替代斷層評估。","textEn":"When handing over fault deformation band demand, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Define fault location and width scenarios from geological evidence, analysing permanent and dynamic demands separately. Special joints or enlarged sections need project review rather than an average-strain substitute for fault assessment.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「斷層變形帶需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault deformation band demand\"?","options":["以地質證據建立可能位置及帶寬情境，將永久位移與動態需求交由結構模型分別處理。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Define fault location and width scenarios from geological evidence, analysing permanent and dynamic demands separately.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以地質證據建立可能位置及帶寬情境，將永久位移與動態需求交由結構模型分別處理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define fault location and width scenarios from geological evidence, analysing permanent and dynamic demands separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b195-v14-28","title":"斷層變形帶需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault deformation band demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷層變形帶需求」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault deformation band demand” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance. Even a large single-joint capacity may not accommodate combined shear and rotation before adjacent lining is damaged. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Even a large single-joint capacity may not accommodate combined shear and rotation before adjacent lining is damaged.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。","textEn":"Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance. Even a large single-joint capacity may not accommodate combined shear and rotation before adjacent lining is damaged.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「斷層變形帶需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault deformation band demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。","只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance.","A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若實際錯動集中於狹窄面，原本分散到長距離的柔性安排可能無效；單一接頭的容量再大也未必容納複合剪切與旋轉，鄰近襯砌可能先受損。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Concentrated offset can defeat flexibility distributed over a long distance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b195-v14-29","title":"串聯柔度分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Series compliance sharing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「串聯柔度分配」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Series compliance sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩個接頭串聯承受相同力而分攤位移，柔度相加不是剛度直接相加。此模型需要相同作用方向且無旁路，土體及其他連接若提供平行路徑必須另建網路。假設k1=100MN/m、k2=50MN/m串聯，keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m；不適用直接並聯相加。串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「串聯柔度分配」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two series joints carry the same force and share displacement; add compliance rather than stiffness. The model assumes one direction without bypasses, while ground or other parallel connections require a different network. For series k1=100MN/m and k2=50MN/m, keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m, unlike a parallel stiffness sum. Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially. The softer joint can take most displacement and fail first while an average stiffness hides controlling seal and connector conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Series compliance sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設k1=100MN/m、k2=50MN/m串聯，keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m；不適用直接並聯相加。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For series k1=100MN/m and k2=50MN/m, keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m, unlike a parallel stiffness sum.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「串聯柔度分配」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Series compliance sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-29-k1","title":"串聯柔度分配","titleEn":"Series compliance sharing","text":"兩個接頭串聯承受相同力而分攤位移，柔度相加不是剛度直接相加。此模型需要相同作用方向且無旁路，土體及其他連接若提供平行路徑必須另建網路。","textEn":"Two series joints carry the same force and share displacement; add compliance rather than stiffness. The model assumes one direction without bypasses, while ground or other parallel connections require a different network.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「串聯柔度分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Series compliance sharing\" is correct?","options":["只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","兩個接頭串聯承受相同力而分攤位移，柔度相加不是剛度直接相加。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Two series joints carry the same force and share displacement; add compliance rather than stiffness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩個接頭串聯承受相同力而分攤位移，柔度相加不是剛度直接相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two series joints carry the same force and share displacement; add compliance rather than stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b195-v14-30","title":"串聯柔度分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Series compliance sharing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「串聯柔度分配」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Series compliance sharing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設k1=100MN/m、k2=50MN/m串聯，keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m；不適用直接並聯相加。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For series k1=100MN/m and k2=50MN/m, keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m, unlike a parallel stiffness sum. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出每個連接的受力路徑並檢查位移相容，用試驗或量測確認同力假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw load paths and displacement compatibility, checking the common-force assumption against tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設k1=100MN/m、k2=50MN/m串聯，keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m；不適用直接並聯相加。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For series k1=100MN/m and k2=50MN/m, keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m, unlike a parallel stiffness sum.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「串聯柔度分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Series compliance sharing\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非現場設定值：假設k1=100MN/m、k2=50MN/m串聯，keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m；不適用直接並聯相加。","只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For series k1=100MN/m and k2=50MN/m, keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m, unlike a parallel stiffness sum.","A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設k1=100MN/m、k2=50MN/m串聯，keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m；不適用直接並聯相加。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For series k1=100MN/m and k2=50MN/m, keq=(1/k1+1/k2)⁻¹=33.3MN/m, unlike a parallel stiffness sum. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b195-v14-31","title":"串聯柔度分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Series compliance sharing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「串聯柔度分配」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Series compliance sharing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出每個連接的受力路徑並檢查位移相容，用試驗或量測確認同力假設。若一處接頭閉合、摩擦鎖定或碰止擋，必須更新等效剛度與變形分配。同時排除以下干擾原因：串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw load paths and displacement compatibility, checking the common-force assumption against tests. Closure, friction locking or a stop at one joint requires updated stiffness and movement allocation. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially. The softer joint can take most displacement and fail first while an average stiffness hides controlling seal and connector conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接串聯柔度分配時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。畫出每個連接的受力路徑並檢查位移相容，用試驗或量測確認同力假設。若一處接頭閉合、摩擦鎖定或碰止擋，必須更新等效剛度與變形分配。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over series compliance sharing, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Draw load paths and displacement compatibility, checking the common-force assumption against tests. Closure, friction locking or a stop at one joint requires updated stiffness and movement allocation.","failure":"注意干擾：串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出每個連接的受力路徑並檢查位移相容，用試驗或量測確認同力假設。若一處接頭閉合、摩擦鎖定或碰止擋，必須更新等效剛度與變形分配。同時排除以下干擾原因：串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。","textEn":"Draw load paths and displacement compatibility, checking the common-force assumption against tests. Closure, friction locking or a stop at one joint requires updated stiffness and movement allocation. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially. The softer joint can take most displacement and fail first while an average stiffness hides controlling seal and connector conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接串聯柔度分配時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。畫出每個連接的受力路徑並檢查位移相容，用試驗或量測確認同力假設。若一處接頭閉合、摩擦鎖定或碰止擋，必須更新等效剛度與變形分配。","textEn":"When handing over series compliance sharing, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Draw load paths and displacement compatibility, checking the common-force assumption against tests. Closure, friction locking or a stop at one joint requires updated stiffness and movement allocation.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「串聯柔度分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Series compliance sharing\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","畫出每個連接的受力路徑並檢查位移相容，用試驗或量測確認同力假設。","只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Draw load paths and displacement compatibility, checking the common-force assumption against tests.","A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"畫出每個連接的受力路徑並檢查位移相容，用試驗或量測確認同力假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw load paths and displacement compatibility, checking the common-force assumption against tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b195-v14-32","title":"串聯柔度分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Series compliance sharing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「串聯柔度分配」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Series compliance sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially. The softer joint can take most displacement and fail first while an average stiffness hides controlling seal and connector conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The softer joint can take most displacement and fail first while an average stiffness hides controlling seal and connector conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要串聯柔度分配符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for series compliance sharing removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。","textEn":"Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially. The softer joint can take most displacement and fail first while an average stiffness hides controlling seal and connector conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「串聯柔度分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Series compliance sharing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串並聯判錯會大幅改變需求分配；較軟接頭可能吃掉大部分位移而先超限，若只用平均剛度，會掩蓋局部止水與連接件的控制情境。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing series and parallel paths changes demand allocation substantially. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b195-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「震後外水壓變化」與「位移容量與交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Post event water pressure change\" and \"Movement capacity and handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b195-v14-33","title":"震後外水壓變化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Post event water pressure change: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「震後外水壓變化」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post event water pressure change” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地震後接頭需同時面對殘餘位移與可能改變的水壓，密封檢核不能只在無水狀態做。靜水壓增量簡單，但裂縫連通、排水損壞及水頭來源須由現場資料確認。假設外側水頭增加Δh=8m，Δu=γwΔh=9.81×8=78.48kPa，約78.5kPa；此為增加值而非總設計水壓。若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「震後外水壓變化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After shaking, joints face residual movement and potentially changed water pressure. Dry testing alone is insufficient; pressure increment is simple, but fracture connections, damaged drainage and head sources need field evidence. For an external head increase Δh=8m, Δu=78.48kPa, about78.5kPa. This is added pressure, not total design pressure. A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers. Concurrent drainage damage can make that leakage more consequential than the initial visible component damage suggests. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Post event water pressure change” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設外側水頭增加Δh=8m，Δu=γwΔh=9.81×8=78.48kPa，約78.5kPa；此為增加值而非總設計水壓。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an external head increase Δh=8m, Δu=78.48kPa, about78.5kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「震後外水壓變化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Post event water pressure change”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-33-k1","title":"震後外水壓變化","titleEn":"Post event water pressure change","text":"地震後接頭需同時面對殘餘位移與可能改變的水壓，密封檢核不能只在無水狀態做。靜水壓增量簡單，但裂縫連通、排水損壞及水頭來源須由現場資料確認。","textEn":"After shaking, joints face residual movement and potentially changed water pressure. Dry testing alone is insufficient; pressure increment is simple, but fracture connections, damaged drainage and head sources need field evidence.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「震後外水壓變化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Post event water pressure change\" is correct?","options":["地震後接頭需同時面對殘餘位移與可能改變的水壓，密封檢核不能只在無水狀態做。","只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["After shaking, joints face residual movement and potentially changed water pressure.","A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地震後接頭需同時面對殘餘位移與可能改變的水壓，密封檢核不能只在無水狀態做。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After shaking, joints face residual movement and potentially changed water pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b195-v14-34","title":"震後外水壓變化：定量估算","titleEn":"Post event water pressure change: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「震後外水壓變化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post event water pressure change” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設外側水頭增加Δh=8m，Δu=γwΔh=9.81×8=78.48kPa，約78.5kPa；此為增加值而非總設計水壓。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an external head increase Δh=8m, Δu=78.48kPa, about78.5kPa. This is added pressure, not total design pressure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：震後對照水位、滲漏與接頭位移，使用核准的壓力及變形組合評估剩餘功能。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After the event, compare water levels, leakage and joint movement against approved combined conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設外側水頭增加Δh=8m，Δu=γwΔh=9.81×8=78.48kPa，約78.5kPa；此為增加值而非總設計水壓。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an external head increase Δh=8m, Δu=78.48kPa, about78.5kPa. This is added pressure, not total design pressure.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「震後外水壓變化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Post event water pressure change\", which statement holds?","options":["只要接頭相對伸長符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","教學假設，非現場設定值：假設外側水頭增加Δh=8m，Δu=γwΔh=9.81×8=78.48kPa，約78.5kPa；此為增加值而非總設計水壓。","只要轉角邊緣張開符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for joint relative extension removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an external head increase Δh=8m, Δu=78.48kPa, about78.5kPa.","A nominal result for rotation induced edge opening removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設外側水頭增加Δh=8m，Δu=γwΔh=9.81×8=78.48kPa，約78.5kPa；此為增加值而非總設計水壓。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For an external head increase Δh=8m, Δu=78.48kPa, about78.5kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b195-v14-35","title":"震後外水壓變化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Post event water pressure change: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「震後外水壓變化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post event water pressure change” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"震後對照水位、滲漏與接頭位移，使用核准的壓力及變形組合評估剩餘功能。檢查排水與備援能力，重啟條件由業主和結構及水工責任人共同確認。同時排除以下干擾原因：若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After the event, compare water levels, leakage and joint movement against approved combined conditions. Check drainage and backup systems; owner, structural and hydraulic leads jointly determine reopening criteria. Also rule out the following competing explanation: A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers. Concurrent drainage damage can make that leakage more consequential than the initial visible component damage suggests. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接震後外水壓變化時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。震後對照水位、滲漏與接頭位移，使用核准的壓力及變形組合評估剩餘功能。檢查排水與備援能力，重啟條件由業主和結構及水工責任人共同確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over post event water pressure change, retain original records, units and reference conditions. After the event, compare water levels, leakage and joint movement against approved combined conditions. Check drainage and backup systems; owner, structural and hydraulic leads jointly determine reopening criteria.","failure":"注意干擾：若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"震後對照水位、滲漏與接頭位移，使用核准的壓力及變形組合評估剩餘功能。檢查排水與備援能力，重啟條件由業主和結構及水工責任人共同確認。同時排除以下干擾原因：若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。","textEn":"After the event, compare water levels, leakage and joint movement against approved combined conditions. Check drainage and backup systems; owner, structural and hydraulic leads jointly determine reopening criteria. Also rule out the following competing explanation: A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers. Concurrent drainage damage can make that leakage more consequential than the initial visible component damage suggests.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接震後外水壓變化時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。震後對照水位、滲漏與接頭位移，使用核准的壓力及變形組合評估剩餘功能。檢查排水與備援能力，重啟條件由業主和結構及水工責任人共同確認。","textEn":"When handing over post event water pressure change, retain original records, units and reference conditions. After the event, compare water levels, leakage and joint movement against approved combined conditions. Check drainage and backup systems; owner, structural and hydraulic leads jointly determine reopening criteria.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「震後外水壓變化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Post event water pressure change\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要連接件局部應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","震後對照水位、滲漏與接頭位移，使用核准的壓力及變形組合評估剩餘功能。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A nominal result for local connector strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","After the event, compare water levels, leakage and joint movement against approved combined conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"震後對照水位、滲漏與接頭位移，使用核准的壓力及變形組合評估剩餘功能。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After the event, compare water levels, leakage and joint movement against approved combined conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b195-v14-36","title":"震後外水壓變化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Post event water pressure change: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「震後外水壓變化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post event water pressure change” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers. Concurrent drainage damage can make that leakage more consequential than the initial visible component damage suggests. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Concurrent drainage damage can make that leakage more consequential than the initial visible component damage suggests.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要震後外水壓變化符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for post event water pressure change removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。","textEn":"A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers. Concurrent drainage damage can make that leakage more consequential than the initial visible component damage suggests.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「震後外水壓變化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Post event water pressure change\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只驗接頭沒有斷裂而忽略外水恢復，密封可能在稍後水頭升高才失效；排水系統同時受損時，漏水後果可能比單一構件損傷更嚴重。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A joint may remain intact yet leak later as water head recovers. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b195-v14-37","title":"位移容量與交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Movement capacity and handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「位移容量與交接」如何影響隧道耐震接頭設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Movement capacity and handover” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic tunnel-joint design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"接頭容量須對應具體運動方向、水壓、老化及循環條件，不能把單軸試驗行程當所有組合的許可值。名義餘量幫助整理，最終仍要查多軸包絡與施工公差。假設同一方向相同試驗條件的容量40mm、需求25mm，餘量40−25=15mm；未包含旋轉、剪切及公差互制。若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「位移容量與交接」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joint capacity belongs to a specified direction, pressure, ageing and cycling condition. A uniaxial stroke is not allowable for every combination; nominal reserve organizes evidence but needs multiaxis and tolerance checks. For capacity40mm and demand25mm in the same direction and test conditions, reserve is15mm, excluding rotation, shear and tolerance interaction. Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion. Initial installation offsets may already consume capacity, so a positive nominal reserve cannot prove post-event sealing or access. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Movement capacity and handover” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設同一方向相同試驗條件的容量40mm、需求25mm，餘量40−25=15mm；未包含旋轉、剪切及公差互制。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For capacity40mm and demand25mm in the same direction and test conditions, reserve is15mm, excluding rotation, shear and tolerance interaction.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「位移容量與交接」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Movement capacity and handover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-37-k1","title":"位移容量與交接","titleEn":"Movement capacity and handover","text":"接頭容量須對應具體運動方向、水壓、老化及循環條件，不能把單軸試驗行程當所有組合的許可值。名義餘量幫助整理，最終仍要查多軸包絡與施工公差。","textEn":"Joint capacity belongs to a specified direction, pressure, ageing and cycling condition. A uniaxial stroke is not allowable for every combination; nominal reserve organizes evidence but needs multiaxis and tolerance checks.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「位移容量與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Movement capacity and handover\" is correct?","options":["只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","接頭容量須對應具體運動方向、水壓、老化及循環條件，不能把單軸試驗行程當所有組合的許可值。","只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Joint capacity belongs to a specified direction, pressure, ageing and cycling condition.","A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接頭容量須對應具體運動方向、水壓、老化及循環條件，不能把單軸試驗行程當所有組合的許可值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joint capacity belongs to a specified direction, pressure, ageing and cycling condition. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b195-v14-38","title":"位移容量與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Movement capacity and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「位移容量與交接」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Movement capacity and handover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非現場設定值：假設同一方向相同試驗條件的容量40mm、需求25mm，餘量40−25=15mm；未包含旋轉、剪切及公差互制。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For capacity40mm and demand25mm in the same direction and test conditions, reserve is15mm, excluding rotation, shear and tolerance interaction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接容量試驗、安裝偏差、監測零點及震後檢查流程，逐項核對設計包絡。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Handover capacity tests, installation deviations, monitoring zeros and post-event procedures against the design envelope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設同一方向相同試驗條件的容量40mm、需求25mm，餘量40−25=15mm；未包含旋轉、剪切及公差互制。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For capacity40mm and demand25mm in the same direction and test conditions, reserve is15mm, excluding rotation, shear and tolerance interaction.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「位移容量與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Movement capacity and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["只要接頭剪切剛度符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","只要止水壓縮幾何餘量符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。","教學假設，非現場設定值：假設同一方向相同試驗條件的容量40mm、需求25mm，餘量40−25=15mm；未包含旋轉、剪切及公差互制。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal result for joint shear stiffness removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","A nominal result for seal compression geometry reserve removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.","Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For capacity40mm and demand25mm in the same direction and test conditions, reserve is15mm, excluding rotation, shear and tolerance interaction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非現場設定值：假設同一方向相同試驗條件的容量40mm、需求25mm，餘量40−25=15mm；未包含旋轉、剪切及公差互制。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not field settings: For capacity40mm and demand25mm in the same direction and test conditions, reserve is15mm, excluding rotation, shear and tolerance interaction. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b195-v14-39","title":"位移容量與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Movement capacity and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「位移容量與交接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Movement capacity and handover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接容量試驗、安裝偏差、監測零點及震後檢查流程，逐項核對設計包絡。任何更換密封或連接件都需確認性能相容，責任工程師簽認後更新文件及警戒值。同時排除以下干擾原因：若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Handover capacity tests, installation deviations, monitoring zeros and post-event procedures against the design envelope. Replacement seals or connectors require compatibility review and engineering approval before documents and alarms are updated. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion. Initial installation offsets may already consume capacity, so a positive nominal reserve cannot prove post-event sealing or access. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接位移容量與交接時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。交接容量試驗、安裝偏差、監測零點及震後檢查流程，逐項核對設計包絡。任何更換密封或連接件都需確認性能相容，責任工程師簽認後更新文件及警戒值。","observationEn":"Site practice: When handing over movement capacity and handover, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Handover capacity tests, installation deviations, monitoring zeros and post-event procedures against the design envelope. Replacement seals or connectors require compatibility review and engineering approval before documents and alarms are updated.","failure":"注意干擾：若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接容量試驗、安裝偏差、監測零點及震後檢查流程，逐項核對設計包絡。任何更換密封或連接件都需確認性能相容，責任工程師簽認後更新文件及警戒值。同時排除以下干擾原因：若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。","textEn":"Handover capacity tests, installation deviations, monitoring zeros and post-event procedures against the design envelope. Replacement seals or connectors require compatibility review and engineering approval before documents and alarms are updated. Also rule out the following competing explanation: Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion. Initial installation offsets may already consume capacity, so a positive nominal reserve cannot prove post-event sealing or access.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接位移容量與交接時保存原始紀錄、單位與基準。交接容量試驗、安裝偏差、監測零點及震後檢查流程，逐項核對設計包絡。任何更換密封或連接件都需確認性能相容，責任工程師簽認後更新文件及警戒值。","textEn":"When handing over movement capacity and handover, retain original records, units and reference conditions. Handover capacity tests, installation deviations, monitoring zeros and post-event procedures against the design envelope. Replacement seals or connectors require compatibility review and engineering approval before documents and alarms are updated.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「位移容量與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Movement capacity and handover\"?","options":["交接容量試驗、安裝偏差、監測零點及震後檢查流程，逐項核對設計包絡。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要斷層變形帶需求符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Handover capacity tests, installation deviations, monitoring zeros and post-event procedures against the design envelope.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A nominal result for fault deformation band demand removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接容量試驗、安裝偏差、監測零點及震後檢查流程，逐項核對設計包絡。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Handover capacity tests, installation deviations, monitoring zeros and post-event procedures against the design envelope. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b195-v14-40","title":"位移容量與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Movement capacity and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"prerequisiteIds":["b195-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「位移容量與交接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Movement capacity and handover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion. Initial installation offsets may already consume capacity, so a positive nominal reserve cannot prove post-event sealing or access. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Initial installation offsets may already consume capacity, so a positive nominal reserve cannot prove post-event sealing or access.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要位移容量與交接符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nominal result for movement capacity and handover removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b195-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。","textEn":"Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion. Initial installation offsets may already consume capacity, so a positive nominal reserve cannot prove post-event sealing or access.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]},{"id":"b195-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「位移容量與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Movement capacity and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。","只要波傳軸向應變符合名義數值，就能略過邊界條件與獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion.","A nominal result for wave induced axial strain removes the need to check boundaries and independent evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若以最大試驗行程減平均需求，可能忽略最不利接頭與多軸組合；施工初始偏差已消耗部分容量時，表面正餘量不能證明震後仍可維持水密與通行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Subtracting mean demand from maximum test stroke misses critical joints and combined motion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa","v14s-seismic-guidance","v14s-bart-seismic","v14s-bart-retrofit","v14s-crossrail-geology"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
